ATT&CK techniques for macOS, made on 12 November 2026 from MITRE's ATT&CK data in STIX 2.1,
https://github.com/mitre-attack/attack-stix-data, release v20.1 (ATT&CK version 20.1 of
5 November 2026), file enterprise-attack/enterprise-attack-20.1.json, whose SHA-256 is
539a843a7b53ed9749740b2123dddae3726b1a4831841c32aca740b011b910b5.

`macos.json` keeps of that file only this: every technique that is neither revoked nor
deprecated and that is for macOS, by its ATT&CK id and name, with a sub-technique folded into
its parent, so a parent is kept when it or one of its sub-techniques names macOS among its
platforms; and the tactics of Enterprise ATT&CK's matrix, in the matrix's order, each with
the kept techniques that serve it. Ids and names are as MITRE publishes them. The program
compiles the file in to draw which techniques the shipped rules cover; nothing fetches it at
run time.

